      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "In this scene, Pavel Osipenko arrives at the office of Governor Viktor Stepanovich to deliver an illicit bribe. Hoping to secure the governor's help against Samsonov, Osipenko hands over a bag full of cash. Cautious about surveillance, the experienced governor insists the bribe is merely three folders of official paperwork. Let's listen to their tense exchange in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Здравствуйте, Виктор Степанович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Что это такое, Павел Юрьевич?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это деньги.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Какие ещё деньги?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Те самые, о которых говорили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "По-моему, вы сильно ошибаетесь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Вы должны были привезти документы.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Вы привезли документы?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, конечно. Три бабки.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Прекрасно! Оставьте эти три папки.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Я посмотрю их позже.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Теперь всё в порядке?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вы поможете разобраться с Самсоновым?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "У нас всё в порядке. Всего доброго!",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's examine the covert bribe delivery line by line. Osipenko and the governor speak in careful bureaucratic code.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Здравствуйте, Виктор Степанович.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Hello, Viktor Stepanovich.' Osipenko enters the governor's office politely.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Что это такое, Павел Юрьевич?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What is this, Pavel Yuryevich?' The governor feigns surprise using polite address.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Это деньги.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This is money.' Osipenko bluntly names the contents of the bag.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Какие ещё деньги?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'What money are you talking about?' The governor immediately questions the phrasing for legal safety.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Те самые, о которых говорили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The very money we talked about.' Osipenko refers back to their previous private agreement.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "По-моему, вы сильно ошибаетесь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'In my opinion, you are sorely mistaken.' The parenthetical word introduces a formal polite denial.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Вы должны были привезти документы.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You were supposed to bring documents.' The modal construction describes expected official paperwork.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Вы привезли документы?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did you bring the documents?' The past tense verb checks whether the paperwork arrived.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Да, конечно. Три бабки.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, of course. Three grand.' Osipenko uses slang that sounds phonetically like folders.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Прекрасно! Оставьте эти три папки.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Excellent! Leave these three folders.' The governor humorously plays along with the phonetic pun.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "Я посмотрю их позже.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will examine them later.' The future perfective verb promises future attention.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Теперь всё в порядке?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Is everything in order now?' Osipenko seeks assurance about their political alliance.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вы поможете разобраться с Самсоновым?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Will you help deal with Samsonov?' Osipenko asks for political retaliation against his rival.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "viktor",
      "t": "У нас всё в порядке. Всего доброго!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Everything is in order with us. Goodbye!' The governor closes the conversation and politely dismisses him. Now let's listen to Osipenko and the governor's coded meeting once more without pauses.",
